{"name":"Summer Sea","hex":"#66a9b1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"summer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of four seasons, traditionally the second, marked by the longest and typically hottest days of the year due to the inclination of the Earth and thermal lag. Typically regarded as spanning  either the period between the summer solstice to the autumnal equinox, or the months of June, July, and August in the Northern Hemisphere and the months of December, January and February in the Southern Hemisphere.","year; used to give the age of a person, usually a young one."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spend the summer, as in a particular place on holiday."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/summer"},{"term":"sea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Semai."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large body of salt water.","The ocean; the continuous body of salt water covering a majority of the Earth's surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Summer","blocks":[{"text":"Summer or summertime is the hottest and brightest of the four temperate seasons, occurring after spring and before autumn. Starting on the summer solstice, daylight hours are the longest and darkness hours are the shortest, with day length decreasing as the season progresses after the solstice. In the Northern Hemisphere, summer is usually defined as starting on June 21 or 22, and ending on September 22 or 23; and in the Southern Hemisphere, as the period between December 22 or 23 and March 20 or 21."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Field_Hamois_Belgium_Luc_Viatour.jpg/330px-Field_Hamois_Belgium_Luc_Viatour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summer","wikidata":"Q1313"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Inari%2C_Finland_-_panoramio_%285%29.jpg/500px-Inari%2C_Finland_-_panoramio_%285%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Inari%2C_Finland_-_panoramio_%285%29.jpg/1280px-Inari%2C_Finland_-_panoramio_%285%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Inari%2C_Finland_-_panoramio_%285%29.jpg/500px-Inari%2C_Finland_-_panoramio_%285%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"During summer in the polar regions, the sun can appear even at midnight. Photo of midnight sun in Inari, Finland.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInari%2C_Finland_-_panoramio_(5).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Darwin_thunderstorm.jpg/500px-Darwin_thunderstorm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Darwin_thunderstorm.jpg/500px-Darwin_thunderstorm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wet season thunderstorm at night in Darwin, Northern Territory, Australia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADarwin_thunderstorm.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Ida_2021-08-29_1321Z.jpg/500px-Ida_2021-08-29_1321Z.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Ida_2021-08-29_1321Z.jpg/1280px-Ida_2021-08-29_1321Z.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Ida_2021-08-29_1321Z.jpg/500px-Ida_2021-08-29_1321Z.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Image of Hurricane Ida from late August 2021.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIda_2021-08-29_1321Z.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Biok%C3%BApalisko_Sninsk%C3%A9_rybn%C3%ADky_011.jpg/500px-Biok%C3%BApalisko_Sninsk%C3%A9_rybn%C3%ADky_011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Biok%C3%BApalisko_Sninsk%C3%A9_rybn%C3%ADky_011.jpg/1280px-Biok%C3%BApalisko_Sninsk%C3%A9_rybn%C3%ADky_011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Biok%C3%BApalisko_Sninsk%C3%A9_rybn%C3%ADky_011.jpg/500px-Biok%C3%BApalisko_Sninsk%C3%A9_rybn%C3%ADky_011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Summer is usually the season of travel, swimming, summer vacation for many people, and also the season for fruits and plants to fully develop.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABiok%C3%BApalisko_Sninsk%C3%A9_rybn%C3%ADky_011.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Atlantic_Ocean_shoreline_in_Myrtle_Beach%2C_South_Carolina.jpg/500px-Atlantic_Ocean_shoreline_in_Myrtle_Beach%2C_South_Carolina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Atlantic_Oc